  "body": "The historical PR503/510 bit R480 word admits a shorter Q-node6 circuit: 51 \u2192 43 XORs, saving 16 complete ADDs after rebuilding literal reverse cleanup. Composing it with the reviewed Q-node2 and Q-node5 circuits reduces the complete word from 33,958 to 33,904 ADDs.\n\nThis is a finite construction and composition certificate. No new \u03ba.\n\n**Exact result**\n\n- Q-node6: phase A, frame 488, original slice [2460,2511), twelve fixed physical outputs.\n- New saving: 16 ADDs. Predecessor savings: 38 ADDs. Combined saving: 54 ADDs.\n- All eight subsets of the three replacements pass complete checks.\n- All 720 persistent register frame paths, 480 helpers, nine COPY/ERASE pairs, and paid rank mass 5,592 remain unchanged.\n- Paid histogram remains {1:1200, 2:1440, 4:180, 6:120, 8:9}.\n- Combined positive bounds: F=176135 and B=3638746, versus baseline B=3751204.\n- Exact combined local payload bound:\n  64 F^3 B^2 = 4630420660642035956595446624000.\n  Every subset uses 102 bits, below the strict 104-bit cap.\n\nAll preparation, source access, frame movement, copy and cleanup operations are charged. These are instruction savings, not measured runtime savings.\n\n**New evidence and attribution**\n\nThe new contribution is the Q-node6 witness and complete admission of all eight compositions. Precision effects are not additive, so each combination is checked separately.\n\nToikY's PR1003 supplies Q-node2 (52 \u2192 43); martinxxx9's PR1089 supplies Q-node5 (51 \u2192 41), the unchanged synthesis algorithm, and reusable replay functions. Their 38-ADD saving is credited separately. No new synthesis algorithm or optimal circuit claim is made.\n\nThe bounded search uses assignment seed 6 and exactly 1,000 trajectories with seed 2026101406. Trial 625 supplies the 43-gate witness. Candidate acceptance checks the complete precision bill in all four predecessor backgrounds.\n\n**Base and pinned dependencies**\n\nStarting commit:\n410026dc5513b87db92ae98571d1d5984c69a983\n\nPR1003:\nb0eda846c34413dabd1e75402b8ad730f8940ff2\n\nPR1089:\n9f33d4d10e59a7575d28378e63c033a4b0c13d3f\n\nOriginal bitE8mut-r480.json.gz SHA-256:\n92e399e9a486b55229b5624632ac54f800dd9e022f2aee97f1e5f264bbc0ef5c\n\nSOURCES.json records SHA-256 and Git blob identities for every consumed dependency. Both predecessor heads were unchanged at the final Git refresh. Public PR/discussion searches found no matching Q-node6 composition; coverage was partial and establishes no priority claim.\n\n**Reproduce**\n\nFrom the repository root, Python 3.11+:\n\n```sh\npython3 -I -B research/r480-qnode6-composition/verify.py --replay-search\n```\n\nExpected final line:\n\n```text\nPASS_R480_QNODE6_COMPOSITION Q6=51->43 ADDs=33958->33904 subsets=8 columns=720 controls=179 no_new_kappa\n```\n\n**Tests executed \u2014 PASS**\n\n- All 4,096 Boolean inputs and inverses for each replacement.\n- All 720 dirty-input columns for every composition.\n- Original H1\u2013H5, PR425 predicates, exact record export and frame accounting.\n- Python and unchanged C++ 5/9/11-stage checks for all eight subsets.\n- 179 Python controls, including every replacement-gate omission, missing compensation, illegal frame descent, endpoint-valid stale cleanup, precision overflow and bridge omissions.\n- 384 native bridge-omission controls.\n- Clean source export without Git metadata, in a path containing spaces, under optimized Python, including native replay.\n- Six package corruption/output-preservation controls.\n- Selected-record integrity and git diff --check.\n\nEnvironment: Linux x86_64, Python 3.12.14, GCC 14.2.0, Boost 1.83. Add --native to the reproduction command for C++ replay; set BOOST_INCLUDE when headers are outside the system include directory.\n\n**Limits**\n\nThis historical bit R480 word is distinct from the current complex provider also called R480. The selected conditional \u03ba remains unchanged at 0.001672660197076918.\n\nNo hosted-parent invoice, selected-frontier cold replay, repository-wide suite, remote CI or Lean proof was run. Boolean equivalence does not assert equality of the old and new integer matrices. All-size compilation, common-label/mutable-source realization, whole-call hosting, uniform precision/tape and analytic transfer remain inherited obligations. No selected certificate, frozen predecessor or upstream/ file is modified.\n\nPrepared for @CubeJerry with substantial OpenAI Codex assistance in research, implementation, verification and writing. Credit also belongs to eumemic, DreamingOfClouds, Dylan Crow, DaysSky, Zhihao Chen and the retained E8 lineage. Original licenses and AI disclosures remain intact; new work is Apache-2.0. No independent human review is claimed.",
